      "title": "Finding the Points on a Curve at which the Tangent Vector is Perpendicular to a Given Vector"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "50921b63-6bdf-5fec-9c29-b3211ea616f0",
      ":question/problem": "At which points on the curve $6 x y + 3 y^{2}=9 x^{2} + 324$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $j$?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $(-3,-9)$\n- **II.** $(0,9)$\n- **III.** $(\\frac{3}{2},9)$\n- **IV.** $(3,0)$\n- **V.** $(3,\\frac{9}{2})$\n- **VI.** $(3,9)$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
